   "lesson": "The clearest round-1 pattern was volatility: range and volatility in AAPL, QQQ, NVDA and MSFT went with up days, which looks like a risk premium and rebounds after stress. Trends over 20 to 60 days reversed, so returns, distance above moving averages and closeness to highs all pointed down, for Apple, the market and the peers alike. Short-term peer and market news worked the other way: overnight gaps, MSFT's close position and returns measured against their own recent history in standard deviations continued into the next day. Apple's moves against the market mostly reversed, except the session return relative to QQQ, which continued."
  },
