   "lesson": "Round 1 showed my instincts were backwards on two points: high volatility and wide ranges (in Apple, QQQ and the peers) precede more up days, not fewer, and long-horizon strength (60-day returns, distance above the 60-day average, closeness to highs) precedes fewer, so Apple mean-reverts at the monthly-to-quarterly horizon and pays a risk premium in turbulent regimes. At the one-day horizon peer and market strength (MSFT return and close position, NVDA and QQQ gaps, NVDA volume) mildly continues into Apple rather than reversing. Apple-specific excess (outperforming QQQ or MSFT, a range or volume spike versus its own norm) mildly reverses, so this batch leans on those consistent multi-year patterns rather than on any single small edge."
  },
