   "lesson": "Round 1 showed that short-horizon volatility and range measures were followed by up days, while longer trend, drawdown and moving-average deviations were followed by down days, which points to mean reversion after extended moves. Apple's own intraday strength and close position within the day were followed by up days, but Apple's short-term outperformance versus QQQ and MSFT was followed by down days. This round I lean on those patterns: volatility and range up, stretched trend or relative strength down, and I use new windows and constructions rather than rewording round-1 factors."
